/* natural-one-attack-god.irh -- fixture for tools/check_natural_one_attack.sh
   (bd inc-bp2y).

   ONE test god. Joining it (wizard mode "Become Divine Champion") throws
   EV_BLESSING once with 30000 favour (src/Debug.cpp:1118-1135), and the
   FAVOUR_CHART below is copied from tools/fixtures/periodic-interval-gods.irh:
   its first rung (1000) sits under 30000 and its second (50000) over it, so a
   fresh follower always lands on level 1 and this handler fires exactly once,
   never again on the same character. The one-shot guard is
   getGodLevel(...)==1, the same gate heal-maladies-god.irh and periodic-
   interval-gods.irh use.

   The blessing grants +30 to hit via GainPermStati(ADJUST_INH, NULL, SS_MISC,
   A_HIT, 30) -- an inherent bonus applied to every hit attribute, the same
   call lib/classes.irh:1055 makes for a mage's saving throw. That is what makes
   the fixture prove the defect: the loaded orc mage has Melee +3, so
   e.vHit + e.vRoll on a forced roll of 1 is 3 + 30 + 1 = 34, comfortably above
   any summoned goblin's Defense. The arithmetic ALONE would hit on a 1, so
   only the natural-1 clause under test can turn that roll into a miss.

   NOT part of the shipped module: tools/check_natural_one_attack.sh splices
   this file onto the END of a scratch copy of lib/main.irc, under logs/, for
   the span of its own run only. No tracked lib/ file is ever touched. */

God "Natural One Attack Test God"
  {
    Lists:
      * FAVOUR_CHART
          1000
          50000
          60000
          70000
          80000
          90000
          100000
          110000
          120000
          130000;
    On Event EV_BLESSING {
      if (EActor->getGodLevel($"Natural One Attack Test God") == 1)
        EActor->GainPermStati(ADJUST_INH,NULL,SS_MISC,A_HIT,30);
      return NOTHING;
      };
  }
